A one-time code entered one character per slot.
[Appica docs](https://appica.dev/ui/components/react/otp-field)

<%= embed UI::OTPFieldPreview, :default %>

## Usage

```ruby
OTPField(length: 6, name: "code", aria_label: "Verification code") do
  6.times { |index| OTPFieldInput(aria_label: "Digit #{index + 1} of 6") }
end
```

Render one `OTPFieldInput` per slot. Typing fills the slots and moves on, Backspace clears and moves back, ←/→ move
between slots, and pasting - or the OS offering an SMS code (`autocomplete="one-time-code"`) - spreads the code
across them. A hidden input submits the joined value under `name:`.

